WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.713
Collection should create both usable material and a trustworthy record of how it was obtained.

00:00:06.713 --> 00:00:11.798
Maintain search notes that link each activity to an information need.

00:00:11.798 --> 00:00:19.731
Record meaningful queries or concepts, source categories checked, dates, and the reason a result was kept or rejected.

00:00:19.731 --> 00:00:28.071
For relevant pages, preserve the URL, title, publisher or account, publication date if available, access timestamp, and source context.

00:00:28.071 --> 00:00:35.190
A screenshot may capture visible content, but it should not replace the URL and surrounding context.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:39.462
Approved archives can help preserve pages that may change.

00:00:39.462 --> 00:00:43.327
Use consistent file names and an evidence register.

00:00:43.327 --> 00:00:48.819
A practical name can include date, source, subject, and a unique identifier.

00:00:48.819 --> 00:00:54.311
Keep original downloads or captures separate from working copies when integrity matters.

00:00:54.311 --> 00:00:58.990
Record transformations such as translation, cropping, transcription, or format conversion.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:02.448
Preserve enough context to avoid misleading excerpts.

00:01:02.448 --> 00:01:09.974
A quotation, image, or statistic may change meaning when separated from its page, date, or prior discussion.

00:01:09.974 --> 00:01:17.500
Note whether the material is a direct observation, a source's assertion, or a copy of another claim.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.551
Follow approved handling and retention rules.

00:01:20.551 --> 00:01:26.450
Restrict sensitive artifacts, protect storage, and document who may access the case material.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:32.349
Do not preserve unrelated personal information simply to make the collection appear comprehensive.

00:01:32.349 --> 00:01:37.028
Collection must remain within lawful public access and authorized methods.

00:01:37.028 --> 00:01:44.147
If a login, technical control, private group, or explicit restriction blocks access, stop and seek guidance.

00:01:44.147 --> 00:01:48.419
OSINT does not provide permission to circumvent the boundary.
